 536:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             /* The following assertion will fail if a service routine (ISR) for
 537:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             an interrupt that has been assigned a priority above
 538:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             configMAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY calls an ISR safe FreeRTOS API
 539:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             function.  ISR safe FreeRTOS API functions must *only* be called
 540:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             from interrupts that have been assigned a priority at or below
 541:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             configMAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY.
 542:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c **** 
 543:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             Numerically low interrupt priority numbers represent logically high
 544:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             interrupt priorities, therefore the priority of the interrupt must
 545:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             be set to a value equal to or numerically *higher* than
 546:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             configMAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY.
 547:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c **** 
 548:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             Interrupts that use the FreeRTOS API must not be left at their
 549:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             default priority of zero as that is the highest possible priority,
 550:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             which is guaranteed to be above configMAX_SYSCALL_INTERRUPT_PRIORITY,
 551:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             and therefore also guaranteed to be invalid.
 552:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c **** 
 553:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             FreeRTOS maintains separate thread and ISR API functions to ensure
 554:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             interrupt entry is as fast and simple as possible.
 555:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c **** 
 556:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             The following links provide detailed information:
 557:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             http://www.freertos.org/RTOS-Cortex-M3-M4.html
 558:Middlewares/Third_Party/FreeRTOS/Source/portable/GCC/ARM_CM4F/port.c ****             http://www.freertos.org/FAQHelp.html */
